{"args":["--project","issue-viewer","show","workflow/local-ci-validate-integrated-main-after-every-merge-and-report-failures"],"pid":3691014,"ppid":3691013,"ts":"2026-10-22T15:28:00Z"}
{"args":["--project","issue-viewer","append","workflow/local-ci-validate-integrated-main-after-every-merge-and-report-failures","--section","Implementation","--body","Built in the design's four steps, one commit each on `work/workflow/local-ci-…`, plus a wording fix:\n1. `1082e2f` **Config and runner.** `internal/tracker/ci.go` (`CIConfig`/`CICommand`: a plain string or a map, lint, schema, `Clone`). `internal/ci/` holds state and run records, the lock, the persistent worktree (guarded so a plain dir never resolves to the main checkout), blame, the runner (process group, timeout, `nice`, filtered env), the watcher and the one-liner. The CLI side is `cmd/issue-cli/cmd_ci.go` (`ci status|run|reset|watch`; `run --detach` puts it in tmux window `ci-\u003cproject\u003e`, kept open after the run, with a `setsid` fallback without tmux) and `ci_report.go` (`ci:` comments, `[from ci]` lead nudge, `on_red: file_issue`).\n2. `88bcea9` **Viewer watcher.** `ci_watch.go` polls every 5 s and spawns `issue-cli ci run --detach --if-untested`, one per repo root; `main.go` starts it in config mode.\n3. `25526c7` **UI.** `ci_view.go` and `status.go`: the Local CI card, the CI row in Waiting on you, `status.md`, and the sidebar count in `nav.go`. `markers.go` adds the `ci-red` chip, which done workboard cards get too. Also the template, CSS, test ids and the legend.\n4. `bf643e6` **Agents and the lead.** The `start` line, the dispatch prompt's `## Local CI` section (through the `tracker.CIStatusLine` hook that `internal/ci` sets, so the server and CLI prompts stay identical), the hint after `transition --to done`, and the lead brief line when `ci:` is set. Turned on in this repo's workflow.yaml (`make validate`, with `ux-test` as the slow tier), with a commented example in the bundled `development` template.\n\n**Deviation from the design:** the bundled template's shipping prompt is push-based, so the \"after the fast-forward\" sentence went only into this repo's workflow.yaml. Every project gets the CLI hint after `transition --to done` and the dispatch prompt section instead, which is the design's preference for CLI output over prompt text.\n\n**Cross-cutting:** no status, transition or overlay changes, and no migration. Without `ci:`, nothing runs, renders or prints (tested). `Clone` copies `ci:` for scoped workflows, and system and type overlays cannot set it. The detached `.worktrees/.ci` is skipped by the branch scan (detached HEAD), and the `ci-\u003cproject\u003e` tmux name is not an agent prefix, so it never shows as an agent. `.ci/` writes its own `.gitignore`."],"pid":3704973,"ppid":3704952,"ts":"2026-10-22T15:28:34Z"}
{"args":["--project","issue-viewer","append","workflow/local-ci-validate-integrated-main-after-every-merge-and-report-failures","--section","Test Plan","--body","**Automated (recorded):** `make validate` is green: vet, `go test ./... -count=1` across all packages, cmd/issue-cli coverage 84.9% (floor 70), playtest-check.\n- `internal/ci` (15 tests, real git in temp repos, fake commands): green, red with test names, timeout kills the group, commits landing mid-run coalesce into one run of the newest head, `--if-untested`, live and stale lock, ignored build output surviving while untracked files are cleaned, `reset`, a plain directory being an error (the main checkout untouched), tiers, blame (ff branch, `--no-ff` merge of a deleted branch, direct commit, rewound branch, first run), red/green streaks, the watcher, the one-liner, the env filter.\n- `internal/tracker`: config parse (string and map), defaults, lint problems, deep `Clone`, failure names, and the lead brief line only with `ci:`.\n- `cmd/issue-cli`: `ci status` text and `--json`, not configured, the red→green cycle with comments and nudges (no repeat while still red), the slow tier, `file_issue` (one issue per streak, updated while red), `--detach`, busy, `reset`, `watch --once`, the `start`/dispatch/`done` lines and their absence without `ci:`.\n- Server: the watcher spawns once per head, deduplicates by repo root and logs an error once; the Status card red, green and absent; `status.md`; the sidebar count; `ci-red` markers on and off.\n\n**Playtest session** `playtest/sessions/local-ci.yaml`, scenario `playtest/scenarios/local-ci`. The viewer's own watcher starts real runs on the scenario's private tmux server, and a tmux action fast-forwards main to a branch that breaks a test. Run it with `make ux-test ISSUE=workflow/local-ci-validate-integrated-main-after-every-merge-and-report-failures`; the owner runs `make playtest ISSUE=…`.\n- [ ] With a ci: block the viewer runs CI on main by itself (tmux session ci-\u003cproject\u003e) and the Status page shows it green\n- [ ] A merge that breaks main turns CI red: card with failing test and merged issue, Waiting on you, sidebar count, ci: comment on the issue, status.md\n- [ ] The merged issue carries a CI red chip on its system page\n- [ ] Agents see the CI state in ci status and in their dispatch prompt (red marked as inherited, never wait)\n- [ ] Sandbox, terminal only: a viewer restart catches up on a head that landed while it was down; the run's tmux session stays open with the result; ci watch works without the viewer; the slow tier runs only on request\n\n**Sandbox for the last box** (`.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh`, gitignored). It holds its own git repo, projects.yaml and branch-built binaries, and talks only to a private tmux server under `TMUX_TMPDIR=/tmp/cisandbox-tmux-$UID` (marker-guarded `clean`). Run every command from the worktree:\n1. `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh setup` should print \"✓ sandbox ready\".\n2. In a second terminal, `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh serve`. Within about 5 s the log shows `ci: cisandbox: new head \u003csha\u003e, run started`. Open http://localhost:18081/p/cisandbox/status: the Local CI card is green.\n3. `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh tmux attach -t ci-cisandbox` shows the run's output ending in `[local CI run finished: press Enter to close]`. Detach with Ctrl-b d.\n4. `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh land-red`. Within about 10 s the card turns red with `make check: TestHeatOverflow, TestCooling` and lists the \"heat\" issue, and `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh cli ci status` starts with `main red since`.\n5. Stop `serve` (Ctrl-C), then run `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh land-fix` while it is down. Start `serve` again: within about 5 s it logs a run for the new head, and the card is green again.\n6. Stop `serve`, `land-red` again, then `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh cli ci watch --once`. It prints `new head …: run started`, and `cli ci status` turns red a few seconds later, with no viewer running.\n7. `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh cli ci run --tier slow` runs `make check` then `make slow`. `cli ci status --tier slow` shows the tier line, and the main state is unchanged by it.\n8. Clean up with `.agent-logs/ci-sandbox/sandbox.sh clean`, which prints \"✓ cleaned\"."],"pid":3705023,"ppid":3704952,"ts":"2026-10-22T15:28:34Z"}
