{"args":["--project","issue-viewer","append","workflow/local-ci-validate-integrated-main-after-every-merge-and-report-failures","--section","Implementation","--body","**Owner playtest follow-up (2026-10-22):** TP5 showed a green card in `make playtest`. In judge mode the runner runs only `setup:`, and the breaking merge was under `act:`, so it never landed. The session now does the wait, the merge and the wait for red in `setup:`. Owner ask: the Local CI card gets a **Last runs** row, the last 12 default-tier runs as boxes (green, red, amber for CI can't run, dashed while running), oldest first, each with a tooltip: commit, result, age, duration and the failing command or tests. Covered by `TestStatusPageShowsLastRuns` and the TP4/TP5 checks."],"pid":890077,"ppid":890064,"ts":"2026-10-22T18:31:39Z"}
